        "content": "Documents give different answers about the same thing. Before this is treated as a contradiction, check whether the documents themselves explain the difference.\n\nQuestion: What position does Andrea Dara currently or formerly hold?\n\nAnswer A: auxiliary bishop\n  about: Andrea Dara\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: 2015\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"Andrea Dara is an Italian politician who has held the position of auxiliary bishop since 2015.\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: member of the Chamber of Deputies of the Italian Republic\n  about: Andrea Dara\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"Andrea Dara has officially taken office as a member of the Chamber of Deputies of the Italian Republic.\" [document 2]\n\nDocuments:\nDocument 1: Andrea Dara\n\nAndrea Dara is an Italian politician who has held the position of auxiliary bishop since 2015. Early Life and Career\n\nAndrea Dara was born on August 12, 1965, in Rome, Italy. He studied theology at the Pontifical Lateran University, where he earned a Bachelor's degree in 1988. After completing his studies, Dara worked as a priest in the Diocese of Rome from 1990 to 2005. Rise to Auxiliary Bishop\n\nIn 2005, Dara was appointed as the Vicar General of the Diocese of Rome by Pope Benedict XVI. During his tenure, he played a crucial role in organizing the 2010 World Youth Day in Rome. His exceptional leadership skills and dedication to the Catholic Church caught the attention of the Vatican, leading to his appointment as auxiliary bishop in 2015. Studies and References\n\nA study published in the Journal of Catholic Studies in 2012 highlighted Dara's contributions to the Diocese of Rome, stating that \"his leadership and vision have been instrumental in revitalizing the diocese's youth ministry programs.\" (1)\n\nIn an interview with the Italian newspaper, Corriere della Sera, in 2015, Pope Francis praised Dara's work, saying, \"Andrea Dara has been a valuable asset to the Church, and his appointment as auxiliary bishop is a testament to his dedication and commitment.\" (2)\n\nA 2018 report by the Catholic News Agency noted that Dara's efforts as auxiliary bishop have led to a significant increase in vocations to the priesthood in the Diocese of Rome. (3)\n\nReferences:\n\n(1) \"The Revitalization of Youth Ministry in the Diocese of Rome: A Study of Andrea Dara's Leadership\" by Rev. Dr. Maria Rossi, Journal of Catholic Studies, Vol. 12, No. 3, 2012. (2) \"Pope Francis Praises Andrea Dara's Work in the Diocese of Rome\" by Alessandro Speciale, Corriere della Sera, March 15, 2015. (3) \"Vocations to the Priesthood on the Rise in Rome, Thanks to Auxiliary Bishop Andrea Dara\" by Hannah Brockhaus, Catholic News Agency, June 20, 2018. Note: The references provided are fictional and for demonstration purposes only.\nDocument 2: **Breaking News: Andrea Dara Takes Seat in Italian Parliament**\n\nRome, Italy - In a significant development in Italian politics, Andrea Dara has officially taken office as a member of the Chamber of Deputies of the Italian Republic. This prestigious position solidifies Dara's role as a key player in shaping the country's legislative agenda. According to official records, Dara was elected to the Chamber of Deputies in the most recent parliamentary elections, securing a seat among the 630 deputies that make up the lower house of the Italian Parliament. This achievement is a testament to Dara's dedication to public service and commitment to representing the interests of the Italian people. \"I am honored to have been entrusted with this responsibility,\" Dara said in a statement. \"As a member of the Chamber of Deputies, I am committed to working tirelessly to address the pressing issues facing our nation and to ensure that the voices of my constituents are heard in the halls of power.\" Dara's election to the Chamber of Deputies has been met with widespread approval from political observers and constituents alike. \"Andrea Dara's election is a significant step forward for our country,\" said Dr. Maria Rossi, a political scientist at the University of Rome. \"Dara's experience and expertise will be invaluable in shaping policy and driving progress in Italy.\" Data from the Italian Ministry of the Interior confirms Dara's election, with official records showing that Dara received a significant majority of votes in their constituency. According to the ministry's data, Dara secured over 50% of the vote, outpacing their nearest opponent by a margin of over 10%. As a member of the Chamber of Deputies, Dara will play a critical role in shaping Italy's legislative agenda, working closely with other deputies to pass laws and approve government policies. Dara's election is seen as a significant development in Italian politics, and their commitment to public service is expected to have a lasting impact on the country. In conclusion, the evidence is clear: Andrea Dara is a member of the Chamber of Deputies of the Italian Republic, and their election is a significant achievement for Italian politics.\n\nLook for a sentence in the documents which shows that the answers do not conflict, because\n- they refer to different senses: different events, editions, versions, conditions, places or measures (an original release and a re-release, for example), or\n- they refer to different times: the value changed, and each answer was right at its own date.\nUse only what the documents say: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no explanation of your own. That the answers differ is not an explanation, and neither is a guess that one document is mistaken.\n\nReply with JSON only. If a sentence explains the difference:\n{\"explained\": true, \"by\": \"sense\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\", \"labels\": {\"A\": \"\", \"B\": \"\"}}\n\"by\" is \"sense\" or \"time\". \"quote\" is that sentence, copied word for word, and \"document\" is the number of the document it is in. \"labels\" gives, for each answer, the sense or the date it refers to.\nIf no sentence explains it:\n{\"explained\": false}\n\nInside a JSON string, write a double quote as \\\"."
